Dataset link : https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/aletbm/aerial-imagery-dataset-floodnet-challenge
The FloodNet Challenge Dataset consists of high-resolution aerial images collected using unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) over flood-affected regions. The dataset was developed to support research in flood detection, damage assessment, and disaster management through computer vision techniques.
The images represent various land-cover and infrastructure categories that commonly appear in flood scenarios. These categories include flooded and non-flooded buildings, roads, vegetation, water bodies, vehicles, and other objects relevant to disaster assessment.
Number of Images: The dataset contains approximately 2,300+ labeled aerial images
Number of Classes
The dataset contains ten classes:
Building Flooded
Building Non-Flooded
Road Flooded
Road Non-Flooded
Water
Tree
Vehicle
Pool
Grass
Flooded Area
Image Type
RGB aerial imagery
UAV/drone-captured images
High-resolution JPEG images
